{%- comment -%}
===============================================================================
  Turn2Opinion — email system v1 ("the conversation")
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Template   : 06. Email change — verify new address
  File       : change-email-verify.liquid
  Class      : Auth (transactional — no unsubscribe)
  Trigger    : Email change approved; verification sent to the new address
  Tone       : blue
  Replaces   : change-email-verify.liquid

  SUBJECT LINES — pick one, or A/B them
    1. Verify your new Turn2Opinion email address
    2. {% assign _nw = user.name.first | default: "" | strip | downcase | split: " " %}{% assign _no = "" %}{% for _w in _nw %}{% if _w != "" %}{% assign _nc = _w | capitalize %}{% if _no == "" %}{% assign _no = _nc %}{% else %}{% assign _no = _no | append: " " | append: _nc %}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if _no != "" %}{{ _no }}{% else %}{% endif %}, one last step to switch your email
    3. Confirm this is your new address

  PREHEADER
    The last step of your email change. Until you verify, the account keeps the old address.

  PRIMARY CTA
    Verify this address  ->  auth/change-email?updatecode=…

  PLAIN-TEXT ALTERNATIVE
    dist/text/change-email-verify.txt — send as the text/plain part of a multipart message.
    HTML-only mail is scored down by most spam filters.

  Generated from react/src/emails/06-change-email-verify.jsx — edit the JSX and re-run
  `npm run build`. Hand edits to this file are overwritten.

  Images are served from the base configured at build time; upload assets/
  there before sending. Serve over HTTPS from a stable path — clients do not
  retry a 404, so a moved asset breaks every copy already delivered.
===============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}
